### 2. Task outcome (extremely detailed version):

DETAILED SCREENING DECISIONS:

INCLUDED STUDIES (5):

Study 21 - CLEAN DELIVERY KIT TRIAL (Tanzania): Randomised stepped-wedge design evaluating clean delivery kits + health 
education delivered via MCHAs and VHWs. Outcomes: cord infection and puerperal sepsis. Meets all criteria.

Study 29 - HOME-BASED NEONATAL CARE (India): Quasi-randomised field trial with comprehensive package including home 
visits, sepsis management, birth asphyxia care, hypothermia management, breastfeeding support, and health education. 
Outcomes: neonatal, infant, and perinatal mortality. Strong match.

Study 37 - COMMUNITY-BASED PERINATAL CARE PILOT (Pakistan): Pilot study with intervention/comparison clusters. Package 
includes LHW training, community education, TBA linkage, and community health committees. Outcomes: stillbirth and 
neonatal mortality. Conservative inclusion due to pilot nature.

Study 39 - TANZANIA CONNECT PROJECT PROTOCOL: Cluster-randomised trial protocol testing Community Health Agents with 
supervisory systems and referral strengthening. Outcomes include maternal/newborn/child health. Inclusion conservative 
given it's a protocol.

Study 40 - PERINATAL AND NEWBORN CARE TRIAL (Pakistan): Cluster-randomised effectiveness trial with comprehensive 
package via LHWs, TBAs, and community health committees. Outcomes: perinatal and neonatal mortality. Strong match.

EXCLUDED STUDIES (15):

Study 22 - Qualitative interview study, not a trial
Study 23 - RCT but outcomes are immunization rates, not mortality/morbidity
