│ intention to treat. The study is registered as ISRCTN65316374. FINDINGS The number of clusters per group was 20,     │
│ with 463 mothers in the intervention group and 440 in the control group. At 6 months, 97 (23%) of 418 and 211 (53%)  │
│ of 400 mothers in the intervention and control groups, respectively, met the criteria for major depression (adjusted │
│ odds ratio (OR) 0.22, 95% CI 0.14 to 0.36, p<0.0001). These effects were sustained at 12 months (111/412 [27%] vs    │
│ 226/386 [59%], adjusted OR 0.23, 95% CI 0.15 to 0.36, p<0.0001). The differences in weight-for-age and               │
